## 🏗️ 1. Reference Architecture Under Analysis

A representative enterprise agentic deployment — the pattern behind most copilots, RPA replacements, and internal "do the whole workflow" agents:

```
                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   TB-1             │              HUMAN PRINCIPAL                 │
  ────────          │        (delegates authority + approves)      │
                    └───────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                                        │  OAuth / delegated identity
                    ┌───────────────────▼──────────────────────────┐
   TB-2             │            ORCHESTRATOR / PLANNER            │
  ────────          │   goal decomposition • routing • budgets     │
                    └──┬──────────────┬──────────────┬─────────────┘
                       │              │              │
        ┌──────────────▼───┐  ┌───────▼───────┐  ┌───▼────────────┐
   TB-3 │  MODEL RUNTIME   │  │  MEMORY LAYER │  │  TOOL LAYER    │
  ──────│  (LLM inference) │  │ RAG • vectors │  │ MCP • APIs     │
        │                  │  │ session state │  │ shell • DB     │
        └──────────────────┘  └───────┬───────┘  └───┬────────────┘
                                      │              │
   TB-4        ┌─────────────────────▼──────────────▼─────────────┐
  ────────     │   UNTRUSTED INGESTION + DOWNSTREAM SYSTEMS       │
               │  documents • email • web • tickets • prod data   │
               └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘
                                      │
   TB-5        ┌─────────────────────▼───────────────────────────┐
  ────────     │        PEER AGENTS (A2A / multi-agent mesh)     │
               └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Trust boundaries

| ID | Boundary | Why it is a boundary | Primary failure mode |
|----|----------|----------------------|----------------------|
| **TB-1** | Human → Agent | Authority is delegated but *not* re-verified per action | Over-delegation; consent laundering |
| **TB-2** | Planner → Executor | Plans are natural language; NL is not an authorization artifact | Goal drift executed with valid creds |
| **TB-3** | Agent → Tool / Memory | Tool descriptors and memory writes are treated as trusted | Poisoned descriptor / poisoned recall |
| **TB-4** | Agent → Untrusted content | Retrieved content enters the same context as instructions | Indirect prompt injection |
| **TB-5** | Agent → Agent | Peer identity is often asserted, not proven | Spoofed agent, transitive privilege |

> **Core modelling principle:** in an agentic system the *context window is a privilege boundary*. Anything that reaches it can influence action. Model it like an untrusted input channel with execution rights, because that is what it is.

