## 🔐 2. STRIDE Decomposition by Component

| Component | **S**poofing | **T**ampering | **R**epudiation | **I**nfo Disclosure | **D**oS | **E**oP |
|-----------|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Orchestrator / Planner** | Fake task source injects goals | Plan rewritten mid-execution | No signed plan lineage | Plan text leaks internal topology | Planning loops burn budget | Planner assumes union of all tool scopes |
| **Model Runtime** | Model substitution / unpinned version | Prompt & system-prompt tampering | Non-deterministic output, no attestation | Training/context leakage | Token exhaustion | Jailbreak unlocks restricted behaviour |
| **Memory / RAG** | Poisoned doc masquerades as authoritative | Vector index poisoning | Memory writes unattributed | Cross-tenant recall | Index flooding | Poisoned memory grants standing instructions |
| **Tool Layer / MCP** | Rogue MCP server impersonates trusted one | Tool descriptor rewritten | Tool calls logged without agent identity | Over-broad reads exfiltrate | Rate-limit exhaustion | Tool chaining composes an unapproved capability |
| **Agent Identity** | Credential reuse across sessions | Token replay | Shared service account = no attribution | Cached creds readable | Auth service flood | Delegation chain escalates silently |
| **A2A Channel** | Unauthenticated peer registration | Message mutation in transit | No message signing | Plaintext inter-agent traffic | Message storm | Peer inherits caller's privileges |
| **Human Interface** | Fake copilot UI | Rationale text manipulated | "The agent decided" — accountability gap | Over-disclosure in explanations | Approval fatigue | Trust exploitation → human executes the attack |

