## 🎯 3. ASI01–ASI10 Control Matrix

Mapping the [OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications 2026](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-for-2026/) to trust boundaries, STRIDE, ATT&CK-style technique classes, and the control that actually reduces the risk (not the one that documents it).

| ID | Risk | TB | STRIDE | Adversary technique class | Primary control (the one that matters) | Residual owner |
|----|------|----|--------|---------------------------|----------------------------------------|----------------|
| **ASI01** | Agent Goal Hijack | TB-4, TB-2 | T, E | Indirect prompt injection via retrieved content | **Provenance-tagged context** — mark every span trusted/untrusted; untrusted spans cannot originate tool calls | Product Sec |
| **ASI02** | Tool Misuse & Exploitation | TB-3 | T, E | Living-off-the-land with granted tools | **Per-tool scoping + argument semantics validation**; destructive verbs require step-up | Platform Eng |
| **ASI03** | Identity & Privilege Abuse | TB-1, TB-5 | S, E | Delegation chain abuse, credential reuse | **Unique bounded agent identity, short-lived creds, no credential passthrough to sub-agents** | IAM |
| **ASI04** | Agentic Supply Chain | TB-3 | S, T | Malicious plugin / typosquatted MCP server | **Signed manifests + AIBOM + registry allowlist**; no runtime discovery of unsigned tools | AppSec / SCM |
| **ASI05** | Unexpected Code Execution | TB-3 | T, E | Generated code executed in-context | **Hard split between generation and execution**; non-root sandbox, no egress by default | Platform Eng |
| **ASI06** | Memory & Context Poisoning | TB-3, TB-4 | T, I | Persistence via long-term memory | **Write-time validation, provenance scoring, TTL decay, no auto-reingestion of agent output** | Data Gov |
| **ASI07** | Insecure Inter-Agent Comms | TB-5 | S, T, I | Spoof / replay / MITM on A2A | **mTLS + signed messages with nonce + schema validation**; authenticated discovery only | Platform Eng |
| **ASI08** | Cascading Failures | TB-2, TB-5 | D | Fault amplification across agent mesh | **Blast-radius caps, circuit breakers, task-scoped one-time creds, replay testing in a digital twin** | SRE + Risk |
| **ASI09** | Human-Agent Trust Exploitation | TB-1 | S, R | Social engineering *through* a trusted agent | **Risk-badged UI, multi-step approval for irreversible actions, immutable rationale log** | Risk + UX |
| **ASI10** | Rogue Agents | TB-2, TB-5 | R, E | Behavioural drift, reward hacking, persistence | **Signed behavioural manifest + watchdog monitoring + kill switch with credential revocation** | AI Governance |

