## ✅ 5. Pre-Deployment Governance Gate

A review board checklist. Every item is binary and evidence-backed — no "in progress" as a passing state.

**Identity & Authorisation**
- [ ] Agent has a unique, non-human identity — not a shared service account
- [ ] Credentials are short-lived and task-scoped; no static secrets in config
- [ ] Sub-agents receive fresh, narrower credentials — never the parent's token
- [ ] Delegation depth is capped and enforced at runtime

**Tools & Execution**
- [ ] Tool inventory is explicit, versioned, and least-privilege scoped
- [ ] Destructive / irreversible actions enumerated and gated behind human approval
- [ ] Code generation and code execution are separated by a validation gate
- [ ] Execution sandbox is non-root, network-egress-denied by default

**Context & Memory**
- [ ] Untrusted content is provenance-tagged and cannot originate tool invocations
- [ ] Memory writes are validated, attributed, and expire on a defined TTL
- [ ] Memory is segmented by user/tenant/task — cross-contamination tested
- [ ] Rollback/snapshot capability exists for suspected poisoning

**Supply Chain**
- [ ] AIBOM exists: models, prompts, tools, MCP servers, datasets, versions pinned
- [ ] All tool descriptors and manifests are signed and verified at load
- [ ] No runtime discovery from unauthenticated registries

**Containment & Oversight**
- [ ] Blast-radius caps and circuit breakers defined per workflow
- [ ] Kill switch tested end-to-end, including credential revocation propagation
- [ ] Tamper-evident logs capture: goal, plan, tool call, arguments, rationale, identity
- [ ] Behavioural baseline established; drift alerting live before go-live

**Governance**
- [ ] AI impact assessment completed (ISO 42001 Cl. 6.1.2)
- [ ] Accountable human owner named — not a team, a person
- [ ] Risk tier assigned; EU AI Act high-risk determination documented
- [ ] Incident runbook covers agent-specific scenarios (rogue agent, memory poisoning, cascade)

